-- title:
--   Modular invariant j as a unit along the special fibre
-- statement:
--   Fix $N \geq 1$ and a prime $p$ with $p \nmid N$, and write $\mathbb{Z}_{(p)}$ for the subring [`GaloisRep.ratLocalizedAt p`](def/GaloisRep_Flat.html#L8) of $\mathbb{Q}$ consisting of the rationals whose denominator is coprime to $p$. Let $c : X \to \operatorname{Spec} \mathbb{Z}_{(p)}$ be a proper smooth morphism of relative dimension $1$ with $X$ integral. The data assumed are: a `CurveModel` $M_0$ for $\mathbb{Q}$ and the modular function field `modularFunctionFieldFull N` $\subset \mathbb{Q}((q))$, i.e. an integral proper smooth curve $M_0.C$ over $\mathbb{Q}$ together with an isomorphism $M_0.\mathrm{ffEquiv}$ onto its function field and a bijection $M_0.\mathrm{placeOfPoint}$ from closed points to places whose stalks realise the corresponding valuation rings, with an isomorphism $e_0$ from $M_0.C$ onto the generic fibre $X \times_{\operatorname{Spec}\mathbb{Z}_{(p)}} \operatorname{Spec}\mathbb{Q}$ over the base; a section $\varepsilon_\infty$ of $c$; a closed point $x_0$ of $M_0.C$ whose place is the $q$-adic cusp `cuspInftyFull N`, together with a $\mathbb{Q}$-point $y$ of the generic fibre lying over $\varepsilon_\infty$ and carried to $x_0$ by $e_0^{-1}$; an analogous model $M_\eta$ over $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ for `modularFunctionFieldBar N` with isomorphism $e_\eta$ onto the $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$-fibre, whose point–place bijection is equivariant for `arithmeticGalois` (hypothesis `hgal`) and compatible with $M_0$ in the sense that pulling back the valuation subring of the place of a $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$-point along `baseChangeEquiv` composed with the right tensor inclusion returns the valuation subring of the place of the specialising closed point (hypothesis `hcompat`); for every valuation subring $A$ of $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ with $p \in A.\mathrm{nonunits}$, a lift $\rho(A)$ of $\mathbb{Z}_{(p)} \to \overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ through $A$, a model $M_s(A)$ over the residue field of $A$ for `modularFunctionFieldFullC`, and an isomorphism onto the corresponding fibre of $c$, all compatible with the base maps; and, when the residue field of $A$ is algebraically closed, a map $r$ on places satisfying `IsPlaceReductionModL` (it preserves degrees and matches orders of reductions of Laurent series) which computes the place of the reduction of any $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$-point obtained from an $A$-point of $X$ (hypothesis `hsp`). Finally let $s$ be a closed point of $\operatorname{Spec}\mathbb{Z}_{(p)}$ such that the image of $x_0$ in $X$ specialises to $\varepsilon_\infty(s)$. The conclusion asserts the existence of two germs $a, b$ in the stalk of $X$ at $\varepsilon_\infty(s)$, neither lying in the ideal generated by the germ there of the global function $p$ (the image of $p \in \mathbb{Z}_{(p)}$ under $c$ on global sections), such that, after specialising to the stalk of $X$ at the image of $x_0$, transporting by the stalk map of $e_0$ followed by the first projection, passing to the function field of $M_0.C$ and applying $M_0.\mathrm{ffEquiv}^{-1}$, the resulting Laurent series satisfy $a = \mathrm{jq} \cdot b$ in $\mathbb{Q}((q))$, where $\mathrm{jq}$ is the $q$-expansion of the modular invariant $j$.
--
--   This records that on a $\mathbb{Z}_{(p)}$-model of the modular curve of level $N$, with $p \nmid N$, the modular invariant $j$ has neither a zero nor a pole along the special fibre: written as a ratio $a/b$ of germs at the special point of the cusp section, both numerator and denominator are prime to $p$, so $\operatorname{div}(j)$ has no vertical component. It is obtained from the variants allowing an integer power of $p$ in the relation, whose positive and negative cases are excluded, and it feeds the construction of a $p$-integral parameter at the cusp on the model.
